To turn this mock-up into a colorful website, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. The jokes written on the notepad can be replaced by actual jokes using a simple script that reads the content from a text file, such as a CSV file or an array.

1. Create a new HTML file and add a basic layout, including a container for the jokes, a container for the reveal button, and a container for the penline button. You can use CSS to style these elements.
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>My Joke Website</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }
    .joke-container {
      margin: 20px 0;
      background-color: #f2f2f2;
    }
    .reveal-button {
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
    .penline-button {
      margin-top: 10px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="joke-container">
    <h1>My Joke Website</h1>
    <p>Type in your joke and push the "Reveal Penline" button below to reveal the punchline!</p>
    <button class="reveal-button">Reveal Penline</button>
    <button class="penline-button">Penline</button>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```
