To turn the mock-up into a colorful and interactive website with a real joke, you can use HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Here's a basic example of what you could create:

HTML:
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>My Joke Website</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <h2>My Joke Website</h2>
  <div class="joke-section">
    <p id="joke-paragraph">
      <span class="punchline"></span>?
    </p>
  </div>
  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```
CSS:
```css
body {
  background-color: #f2f2f2;
}

h2 {
  color: #2c3e50;
  font-size: 24px;
  margin: 20px 0;
  text-align: center;
}

.joke-section {
  margin: 20px 0;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 5px;
}

.punchline {
  color: #ff3b30;
}
```
JavaScript:
```javascript
const punchline = "Push to reveal punchline?";

const punchlineElement = document.getElementById("punchline");

punchlineElement.textContent = punchline;

document.addEventListener("click", function() {
  if (punchlineElement.textContent === punchline) {
    punchlineElement.textContent = "Funny joke";
  }
});
```
This example will create a colorful and interactive website with a real joke hidden behind a punchline. When the user clicks on the punchline, the joke will be revealed.
